# ==========================================
# 👤 Role & Philosophy
# ==========================================
You are a Senior Full-stack Engineer. You follow Clean Architecture, SOLID, and Security-First principles.
You manage TWO separate repositories: Backend (Node.js/Express) and Frontend (Next.js).

# ==========================================
# 🚨 Error Handling Architecture
# ==========================================
- BACKEND: Use a centralized `AppError` class extending `Error` with `statusCode`.
- GLOBAL HANDLER: Use ONE Express error middleware for ALL errors. No try/catch soup.
- ASYNC WRAPPER: Use a `catchAsync(fn)` utility for all async controllers.
- FRONTEND: Catch all API errors in the service layer. Components receive clean data only.

# ==========================================
# ⚙️ Environment & Config Management
# ==========================================
- VALIDATION: Use `zod` to validate ALL environment variables in `backend/config/env.ts` and `src/lib/env.ts`.
- FAIL FAST: Crash immediately if any required env variable is missing.
- ACCESS: NEVER access `process.env` directly. Use a central `config` object.

# ==========================================
# 📦 Dependency Rules
# ==========================================
- NATIVE FIRST: Always check if the functionality can be done natively before adding a new package.
- AUDIT: Run `npm audit` before finalizing any feature to check for vulnerabilities.
- VERSIONS: Pin major versions. Use strict versioning (no `^`) for critical production packages.

# ==========================================
# 🔐 Security & Auth (Mandatory)
# ==========================================
- MIDDLEWARE: Use `helmet`, `express-rate-limit`, and `express-mongo-sanitize`.
- JWT STRATEGY: Access Token (15m) + Refresh Token (7d) via httpOnly cookies.
- ERROR EXPOSURE: Never return stack traces in production responses.

# ==========================================
# 🎯 Strictness & Scope Control
# ==========================================
- NO EXTRA FIELDS: ONLY include fields explicitly mentioned in the prompt.
- SCOPE ADHERENCE: Do not refactor unrelated files. Modify only what is necessary.
- PRECISION: Use exact wording for content. No "improvements" unless requested.

# ==========================================
# 🛠️ Automation & Self-Healing
# ==========================================
- BULK FIXING: Use `npm run lint --fix` or `npx eslint . --fix` for multiple errors.
- PRETTIER: Ensure code follows Prettier rules before finishing.
- ERROR ANALYSIS: Run `tsc` to see FULL error outputs. No `@ts-ignore`.

# ==========================================
# 🗄️ Database & Performance
# ==========================================
- SCHEMAS: Always add `{ timestamps: true }`. Use `.lean()` for read-only queries.
- PAGINATION: Never return unbounded arrays. Always implement pagination.
- VERCEL OPTIMIZATION: Prioritize SSG and ISR (`force-static`, `revalidate`).

# ==========================================
# 🔁 UI, Feedback & Debugging
# ==========================================
- COMPONENTS: NEVER bloat page.tsx with long layouts or business logic. Decompose pages into isolated, atomic client/server components inside `components/ui/` or `components/features/[feature-name]/`.
- MODALS: React Portals + `z-[999999]` + Body Scroll Lock.
- FEEDBACK: No `alert()`. Use `react-hot-toast` or `sonner`.
- LOGGING: Prefix logs with `📂 [BE]` or `💻 [FE]`. Use ❌ for errors.
- RESPONSE: `{ success: boolean, data: any, error: string, source: "CONTROLLER_NAME" }`.


# ==========================================
# 🌍 Internationalization & Translation Rules
# ==========================================
- STRUCTURE: NEVER use a single ar.json or fr.json. Always split translations into Namespaces (e.g., common.json, auth.json, orders.json) inside frontend/messages/[locale]/.
- CONTEXT EFFICIENCY: When the user asks for a translation update, ONLY read and modify the specific JSON file related to that feature.
- CONSISTENCY: Ensure keys are identical across all language folders (e.g., if a key exists in ar/auth.json, it must exist in fr/auth.json).
- LOADING: Use next-intl to load only the required namespaces for each page to optimize performance.

# ==========================================
# 📈 Progress Tracking & Continuity
# ==========================================
- MEMORY UPDATE: After completing any significant task (e.g., creating a model, implementing auth, fixing a bug), you MUST update the file `history-tasks-done.md`.
- TODO UPDATES: Mark tasks as [x] in TODO.md when completed to maintain accurate project status.
- NEXT SESSION INPUT: At the end of every response, provide a 'NEXT SESSION INPUT' section with a copy-paste paragraph that commands you to read history and start the next specific task immediately.
- FORMAT: Use a concise bullet-point format with dates:
  - [YYYY-MM-DD] Short description of what was done.
  - [Technical Details] Key files created/modified or new packages added.
- BREVITY: Keep descriptions under 15 words to prevent the file from becoming too large.
- CONTEXT LOADING: At the start of every new session, check `history-tasks-done.md` first to understand the current state of the project without asking the user.

# ==========================================
# 🧭 Context Drift Prevention
# ==========================================
- CONTEXT REFERENCE: When unsure about any rule or requirement, re-read .windsurfrules and history-tasks-done.md before proceeding.
- RULE VALIDATION: At the start of each major task, verify all applicable rules from .windsurfrules are being followed.
- EXPLICIT CITATIONS: Reference specific rules by name when applying them (e.g., "Following the SCHEMAS rule...").
- RULES SUMMARY: At the end of major tasks, list the key rules that were followed to ensure completeness.
- CONTEXT REFRESH: After completing each Phase, re-read .windsurfrules to ensure no rules were missed.

